# Terraform / OpenTofu
**/.terraform/
**/.terraform.lock.hcl
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.backup
*.tfplan
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json

# Helm — exclude downloaded charts but keep dfe-common library chart
# (ArgoCD needs the packaged library chart since it can't resolve file:// deps)
**/charts/*.tgz
!helm/charts/*/charts/dfe-common-*.tgz

# Secrets / certs
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Scratch / temp
.tmp/

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# AI agent working files (not committed)
docs/superpowers/

# OS junk (never useful in repo)
Thumbs.db
*.swo
*~

# Local environment files (never commit -- contain secrets)
!.env.example.*

# Local working files (not committed)
#
# Authoritative protection for hyperi-ai content is .git/info/exclude
# (per-repo, never committed). The entries below ALSO appear there;
# duplicating them in .gitignore is belt-and-braces -- if a developer
# uses a tool that doesn't respect .git/info/exclude (unusual), the
# .gitignore still catches it. We do not RELY on these being committed
# in .gitignore -- attach surgically appends them if missing, leaves
# them alone if already present.
.mcp.json
.ai-version

# hyperi-ai per-project context + tool-specific equivalents.
# Real files in project tree (Claude Code / Codex / Gemini / Cursor
# all load these from project root natively). Local-only, never
# committed -- mirrored in .git/info/exclude.
CLAUDE.md
TODO.md
AGENTS.md
GEMINI.md
.claude/
.codex/
.cursor/
.gemini/
.cursorrules

# Git worktrees (local dev convenience)
.worktrees/

# Local scratch / tmp (CORE.md: scratch goes here, gitignored, NOT
# /tmp). Bare patterns (no leading slash) match a tmp dir at ANY
# depth, so these cover top-level .tmp/ and tmp/ as well as nested
# ones like tests/tmp/. Mirrored in attach.py _DEFAULT_EXCLUDES.
tmp/
